// control-h0-r1known twin (t_96daf53b): sd_h0_r1known.fcg at fp32 output.
//
// TWO source differences, not one - the declaration (out float4 against out
// half4) and the explicit (half4) cast the H0 side needs on its store.
// sd_h0_nodepth's pair is the one-token pair; this one is not, and the claim
// that matters is not about the sources anyway: the two CONTAINERS differ in
// the outputFromH0 flag and in the destination register of the last
// instruction, two bytes of 272, because the body is fp32 on both sides.  The
// arithmetic, the registers and the live R1 are identical.
//
// So the SDK builds a different control word for this side and nothing else
// about the two programs differs.  Its zeta is the expectation the H0 side is
// judged against: the vertex program's own Z on all 4096 pixels.  If the H0
// side ever reads the ramp described in sd_h0_r1known.fcg instead, the bind
// has started exporting depth for a program that declares none.
void main(float4 t : TEXCOORD0, out float4 o : COLOR)
{
    float4 f = t * 0.5 + float4(0.125, 0.25, 0.375, 0.5);
    float4 g = f * f + t;
    o = g * 0.25 + f;
}
